From 3405a40eee7585b04a31725a0b089d12f866cec7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dotheroes <dotheroes@localhost>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 02:43:44 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 74/75] Photo utilities: cellPhotoExport, cellPhotoImport,
 cellPhotoDecode

The three were placeholders with made-up functions, so a title's imports
stayed unresolved. Now the SDK's functions, each answering through the
title's finish callback (cellSysutilQueueGuestCallbackArgs):

- export (cellPhotoUtility): Initialize/Initialize2/Finalize/Progress, and
  FromFile/FromFileWithCopy copying the title's picture into the photo
  column's folder, <PS3_HDD0_ROOT>/photo (numbered when the name is taken);
- import (cellPhotoImportUtil): cellPhotoImport/cellPhotoImport2 pick the
  newest JPEG or PNG there (or PS3_PHOTO_IMPORT=<host file>), copy it into
  the title's directory and fill CellPhotoImportFileData -- or answer
  RET_CANCEL, the player backing out, when there is none;
- decode (cellPhotoDecodeUtil): FromFile decodes with stb_image into the
  title's RGBA buffer, scaled down to fit with its aspect kept.

3D Dot Game Heroes' ALBUM waited on a black screen for the import's
callback for good; it now shows the newest picture, or backs out.
